From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: client pattern objects (UiaGetPatternProvider and 28 pattern methods), UiaSetFocus, MSAA proxy properties

UiaGetPatternProvider, UiaPatternRelease, UiaSetFocus and the Invoke, ExpandCollapse,
Toggle, Value, RangeValue, SelectionItem, ScrollItem, Scroll, Dock, Transform, Window,
VirtualizedItem, MultipleView, SynchronizedInput and LegacyIAccessible pattern methods
were spec stubs. A pattern object remembers the node and the index of the provider
that has the pattern; every call goes to that provider through a new
IWineUiaProvider::call_pattern method so that it runs in the provider's apartment
(or process, through the nested node provider), where the pattern provider
interface is asked for and called. Unsupported patterns give S_OK and no object,
a pattern object used with another pattern's method is E_INVALIDARG, a provider
object without the interface is UIA_E_NOTSUPPORTED, and the provider's HRESULT
is returned. The Grid and ItemContainer methods and the text pattern remain stubs.

The proxy that UiaProviderFromIAccessible makes now answers BoundingRectangle,
ProcessId, ClassName (for the window itself), HelpText, AccessKey and the
LegacyIAccessible Name, Value, Description, Role, State, Help, KeyboardShortcut,
DefaultAction and ChildId properties instead of leaving them unimplemented.
